    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Phormium colensoi</b></i> (syn. <i>Phormium cookianum</i>; <b>mountain flax</b>, <b>lesser New Zealand flax</b>, or <b>wharariki</b> in Māori) is a perennial plant that is native to New Zealand. It is less common than the other <i>Phormium</i> species, <i>P. tenax</i>. The greenish, yellow or orange flowers are followed by twisted seed pods.",
